== Preparation ==

> The cooking goes fast, and you have to work quickly to not burn things and make them bitter. Thus, we specifically call out all prep here so you can work quickly and efficiently.

Prepare @silken tofu{1%lbs}(cut into 1-inch cubes).

In a #bowl, prepare @scallion{1}(finely chopped).

In a #bowl, prepare @ginger{3%tbsp}(skinned and finely minced).

In a #bowl, prepare @garlic{3%tbsp}(finely minced).

Prepare @Sichuan peppercorns{1%tbsp}(finely ground, for milder flavor use only 1 tsp).

Measure @chicken broth{2/3%cup}(substitute water if desired).

In a #small bowl{}, combine @water{1/4%cup} and @cornstarch{1.5%tsp}.

== Homemade Chili Oil ==

Heat your #wok{} or a small saucepan over low heat. Add @oil{1/4%cup} and throw in @thai chili peppers{2}(technically thai bird chili peppers, thinly sliced) and @red chilies{7}(dried, roughly chopped). Stir occasionally and heat until fragrant, about ~{5%minutes}, ensuring that the peppers don't burn. Remove from heat and set aside in a #bowl, with all the oils included.

== Putting it All Together ==

In the same wok, heat @oil{1/4%cup} over medium heat.

Add ginger. 

After ~{1%minute}, add garlic. 

Fry for another ~{1%minute}, and then turn up the heat to high and add @ground pork{8%ounces}. Break up the meat and fry it until it's cooked through. 

Add Sichuan peppercorns and stir for about ~{15-30%seconds}, taking care to not let it burn, as it will turn bitter if it does.

Add @spicy bean sauce{1.5%tbsp} to the mixture and stir it in well. 

Add chicken broth to the wok and stir. Let this simmer for about ~{1%minute}. 

Add the cornstarch mixture to your sauce and stir. Let it bubble away until the sauce starts to thicken. If it gets too thick, splash in a little more @?chicken broth{}(alt. water for ease).

Then add your chili oil from before. Stir the oil into the sauce, and add the tofu. Use your spatula to gently toss the tofu in the sauce. Let everything cook for about ~{3-5%minutes}. 

> Avoid tossing the tofu too much or too rough, or you'll start breaking it up.

Add @?sesame oil{1/4%tsp} and @?sugar{1/4%tsp} along with the scallion and stir until the scallions are just wilted.

Serve with a last sprinkle of @?Sichuan peppercorns{1/4%tsp} as a garnish if desired.